<%- include('partials/header') %>

<section class="hero">
  <h1>Know your chemistry <span class="accent">before the first date</span></h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Kindred builds a rich personality profile from your social presence and a science-informed
    questionnaire — then gives you a personal QR code. Scan someone else's code and get an instant,
    honest read on your romantic compatibility, with practical advice on how to be great together.
  </p>
  <div class="cta-row">
    <a class="btn btn-lg" href="/register">Create your profile</a>
    <a class="btn btn-lg btn-ghost" href="/login">I already have one</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="features">
  <div class="card feature">
    <div class="feature-icon">🪞</div>
    <h3>A profile that's actually you</h3>
    <p>Link your LinkedIn and socials, paste your bios and posts, and answer a Big Five personality,
       attachment-style, values and love-language questionnaire. Kindred blends it all into one profile.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card feature">
    <div class="feature-icon">📱</div>
    <h3>Your personal QR code</h3>
    <p>Every account gets a unique QR code. Show it at a party, on your dating profile, or on your phone's
       lock screen. One scan is all it takes.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card feature">
    <div class="feature-icon">💘</div>
    <h3>Real compatibility insight</h3>
    <p>A weighted score across values, personality, attachment, interests, love languages and lifestyle —
       plus concrete "how to partner each other" advice, not just a number.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="how card">
  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><strong>Sign up</strong> and build your profile — socials, personality questions, values, interests.</li>
    <li><strong>Get your QR code</strong> on your dashboard, ready to show anyone.</li>
    <li><strong>Scan theirs</strong> with your camera (or type the code) when you meet someone interesting.</li>
    <li><strong>Read your report</strong>: a compatibility score, your strengths as a pair, watch-outs, and tailored advice.</li>
  </ol>
</section>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
